  "notes": "The retro-soul pole of the lane, and the entry names the drum sound rather than the drummer: \"the Dap-Kings kit is the parameter — a dry, dead, close-mic'd 60s kit with heavy damping, snare cracked hard on 2 and 4, no hat carpet, tambourine and handclaps doubling the backbeat, and Motown-style triplet or 16th-note march fills into sections\". So the velocity tiers are the hardest of any model in this section, the kick is on 1 and 3 at a syncopation of 0.18, the hat is neither continuous nor busy (fill density 0.12), the tambourine mirrors the clap and the percussion sits only 2 dB down, and the snare rolls are triplet-and-16th march figures. The band is the sourced 70–103 for the mid-tempos. Harmony is the entry's two-album split held in one model: album one is \"jazz-harmonic… with ii–V–I turnarounds, tritone subs and passing diminisheds\" and album two is \"girl-group diatonic… built on `i–VI–III–VII` and `I–vi–IV–V`\" — all three families are written out by the research, and `susOrDimProb` carries the passing diminisheds. Melody is \"low contralto with heavy behind-the-beat placement, blues thirds, big pitch bends\", hence the lowest flagship register here and a raised `halfStepDissonance`; the backgrounds are \"male-and-female group-vocal answers to the lead line rather than stacks of her own voice\", which is why the counter is an `answer_lick` at −12 rather than an octave stack. Bass is \"upright bass on album one, played electric bass on album two — Jamerson/Motown 8th-note melodic lines with chromatic approach notes… Never an 808 and never a sub\", so no `bass808` block exists and the passing-tone set is chromatic. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability and velocity band and all melody/countermelody numbers. ⚠ **\"Back To Black\" reads both 123 and 62 in the source data because the kit plays a half-time backbeat over a 123 pulse.** That device is documented as \"the single most-copied arrangement device in this lane\" but it is not encoded: the Lane line's spine for the catalogue is straight 2&4, and one model states one placement.",
